From: Yevhen Salitrynskyi <ysalitrynskyi@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 5 Nov 2026 17:48:42 -0500
Subject: fix: open what a page opens in a Space with its own session

The browser's own pages live in the profile's jar, and a tab opened from one in
a Space with an Independent session starts there too. A moment after it arrived
the Space moved it to its own jar. Its contents were replaced before the page it
was opened for had started, so the page never came: an extension's Website
settings, a window.open from chrome://extensions, stayed an empty tab.

A tab a page opened now keeps its contents while it has no page. A settings page
stays in the profile's jar, and a web page moves to the Space's jar as its
navigation starts, with its address, as SpaceJarNavigationThrottle does for
every other tab.

This reproduces one half of the report, and only in a Space with its own
session. Manage extension did not fail here through chrome::ShowExtensions, from
such a Space or any other, so the rest stays open for the Mac.

Why: an extension's settings could not be reached from such a Space (BACKLOG
S-432, GitHub issue 79, sessions S37).

Removable when: a Space's tabs are not moved between jars after they are made.
---
 chrome/browser/ui/spaces/space_model.cc       |  11 ++
 chrome/test/stedding/BUILD.gn                 |   1 +
 .../stedding/extension_pages_browsertest.cc   | 137 ++++++++++++++++++
 3 files changed, 149 insertions(+)
 create mode 100644 chrome/test/stedding/extension_pages_browsertest.cc

diff --git a/chrome/browser/ui/spaces/space_model.cc b/chrome/browser/ui/spaces/space_model.cc
index 17004736f6341..ce9e87561df41 100644
--- a/chrome/browser/ui/spaces/space_model.cc
+++ b/chrome/browser/ui/spaces/space_model.cc
@@ -3521,6 +3521,17 @@ void SpaceModel::MaybeRebindTabJar(tabs::TabInterface* tab) {
                        }
                        content::WebContents* const contents =
                            tab->GetContents();
+                       // sessions S20 (BACKLOG S-432, GitHub issue 79): a tab a
+                       // page opened waits for that page, and new contents
+                       // would never get it: the browser's own pages live in
+                       // the profile's jar, so what chrome://extensions opened
+                       // in a Space with its own session stayed an empty tab.
+                       // SpaceJarNavigationThrottle moves it, with its
+                       // address, if the page belongs elsewhere.
+                       if (contents && contents->HasOpener() &&
+                           HasNoPageOfItsOwnYet(contents)) {
+                         return;
+                       }
                        const SpaceId id = model->SpaceForTab(tab);
                        if (!NeedsOtherJar(contents,
                                           contents ? contents->GetVisibleURL()
